WEBVTT

00:00:01.340 --> 00:00:04.890
IN MAGMELL
SEVENTH WARD RESEARCH FACILITY

00:00:11.350 --> 00:00:13.730
-The time has arrived.
-Yes.

00:00:14.650 --> 00:00:18.360
If we succeed, modern medical science
will be changed forever.

00:00:20.690 --> 00:00:24.110
Will you be able to rest once
this phase of the research is complete?

00:00:24.740 --> 00:00:26.490
Yes. I plan to.

00:00:27.370 --> 00:00:29.030
I'm sure your daughter will be delighted.

00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:32.080
We'll see.

00:00:33.040 --> 00:00:34.460
She's at the age

00:00:34.870 --> 00:00:38.130
where she values spending time
with her boyfriend over her father.

00:00:43.840 --> 00:00:44.680
What happened?

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:46.130
They're...

00:02:25.820 --> 00:02:30.320
RULER OF THE 7TH WARD

00:02:33.160 --> 00:02:34.030
It's all right.

00:02:39.120 --> 00:02:41.790
You're not in despair just yet.

00:02:42.920 --> 00:02:43.750
Despair?

00:02:45.340 --> 00:02:46.960
It's what lies beyond hope...

00:02:48.470 --> 00:02:49.300
perhaps.

00:02:50.840 --> 00:02:51.800
Hope...

00:03:05.270 --> 00:03:06.110
Sir.

00:03:13.240 --> 00:03:15.030
Is this despair?

00:03:34.090 --> 00:03:37.510
KUSK ARCHIPELAGO

00:04:01.830 --> 00:04:05.830
DRIFT

00:04:14.800 --> 00:04:15.640
What's this?

00:04:16.430 --> 00:04:19.470
If something happens to me, go to him.

00:04:31.360 --> 00:04:32.900
Excuse me...

00:04:34.820 --> 00:04:37.120
Another fertile-chested customer?

00:04:38.700 --> 00:04:40.370
What kind of request do you have?

00:04:41.580 --> 00:04:43.460
There's someone I want you to save.

00:04:45.120 --> 00:04:46.080
Please come in.

00:04:53.670 --> 00:04:55.630
I got the worst possible luck...

00:04:57.140 --> 00:04:59.390
Sir, we have a customer.

00:05:03.810 --> 00:05:06.940
<i>This is... the legendary Angler...</i>

00:05:08.770 --> 00:05:09.940
Pleased to meet you.

00:05:13.320 --> 00:05:15.650
-I see.
-Yes...

00:05:16.280 --> 00:05:18.490
You want me to save your father.

00:05:19.120 --> 00:05:23.540
Yes. Communications from the research
facility my father was at have ceased.

00:05:23.870 --> 00:05:25.790
What kind of research does he do?

00:05:26.790 --> 00:05:30.710
He's the head of Kyokusei's
practical lifeform research department.

00:05:32.050 --> 00:05:34.510
Wouldn't a big company like Kyokusei

00:05:34.590 --> 00:05:36.720
have their own private rescue
party for cases like this?

00:05:37.380 --> 00:05:39.930
-Yes...
-Then why don't you leave it to them?

00:05:40.600 --> 00:05:41.970
My father instructed me

00:05:42.560 --> 00:05:45.680
to come here if anything
ever happened to him.

00:05:48.100 --> 00:05:51.440
-Do you have some connection with--?
-Not that I remember.

00:05:53.980 --> 00:05:56.700
-Maybe this is some kind of punishment.
-What?

00:05:57.240 --> 00:06:01.450
It's rather arrogant to use a life
solely for the benefit of humans.

00:06:02.160 --> 00:06:06.200
-I want no part in this. Try elsewhere.
-But--!

00:06:07.210 --> 00:06:08.960
My father raised me by himself...

00:06:09.830 --> 00:06:12.210
If I lose him... I'll...

00:06:13.040 --> 00:06:16.130
Not an uncommon circumstance.
You and everyone else.

00:06:18.760 --> 00:06:19.590
That's horrible...

00:06:20.340 --> 00:06:21.680
It's reality.

00:06:41.820 --> 00:06:42.740
Please.

00:06:43.780 --> 00:06:46.450
You're the only person
I can entrust with this.

00:06:46.540 --> 00:06:47.540
Mr. Shuin!

00:06:57.760 --> 00:07:00.840
I'm Inyo, not Shuin.

00:07:00.930 --> 00:07:04.140
What? But I'm sure this was the place...

00:07:04.850 --> 00:07:07.560
-I'll take your request.
-Really? But...

00:07:10.100 --> 00:07:13.230
Anything Shuin can do,
I can do just as well.

00:07:15.570 --> 00:07:16.480
Wait!

00:07:34.460 --> 00:07:36.090
Miss Emilia!

00:07:36.800 --> 00:07:37.800
Who's this?

00:07:38.840 --> 00:07:41.510
He's my... little brother.

00:07:43.090 --> 00:07:45.510
Please take care of our father.

00:07:46.140 --> 00:07:47.890
No need for concern.

00:07:48.260 --> 00:07:50.980
No matter where our company's
prized <i>Sky Whale 7</i> may fly,

00:07:51.060 --> 00:07:53.730
it's like nothing more
than having a little picnic.

00:07:53.980 --> 00:07:54.810
Well then.

00:07:59.030 --> 00:08:01.320
Who are you calling little brother?

00:08:02.200 --> 00:08:04.740
I can't bring outsiders along.

00:08:04.820 --> 00:08:07.740
And based on your height,
little brother seemed the most...

00:08:08.660 --> 00:08:09.700
Be careful.

00:08:11.330 --> 00:08:13.210
There's this jinx that

00:08:13.670 --> 00:08:16.290
if you mention my height,
your helicopter will crash.

00:08:35.190 --> 00:08:37.900
-<i>Zero.</i>
-Yes! Sir!

00:08:38.570 --> 00:08:41.190
<i>Go ahead of us and do</i>
<i>reconnaissance of the site.</i>

00:08:41.280 --> 00:08:42.280
Understood.

00:09:25.150 --> 00:09:26.320
They were annihilated.

00:09:30.240 --> 00:09:31.450
<i>Emilia...</i>

00:09:37.750 --> 00:09:41.040
<i>Entering Magmell airspace.</i>
<i>Level three preparations.</i>

00:09:42.050 --> 00:09:43.880
<i>Level three preparations initialized.</i>

00:09:45.470 --> 00:09:50.390
The Kel-Bear. It's normally
a gentle animal that feeds upon minerals.

00:09:50.800 --> 00:09:53.600
However, when angered,
its skin turns to steel

00:09:53.680 --> 00:09:55.600
and it becomes uncontrollably violent.

00:09:56.680 --> 00:10:00.360
Presently, the research facility
is surrounded by 30 Kel-Bears.

00:10:01.440 --> 00:10:03.150
The situation has become dire.

00:10:04.860 --> 00:10:09.360
Well, that is... until we arrive on site.

00:10:12.780 --> 00:10:14.120
950,000 people.

00:10:15.830 --> 00:10:18.710
The number of people that
go missing in Magmell each year.

00:10:19.540 --> 00:10:22.630
A third of those never return alive.

00:10:23.420 --> 00:10:26.170
Of course, that includes
armed individuals as well.

00:10:26.260 --> 00:10:27.630
You know your stuff.

00:10:28.720 --> 00:10:30.640
Good on you for studying so hard.

00:10:31.510 --> 00:10:35.720
Rest assured. We will make sure
we're in the other two-thirds.

00:10:41.980 --> 00:10:43.440
Professor! The rescue party!

00:11:01.420 --> 00:11:04.420
-How intriguing.
-Isn't it?

00:11:04.840 --> 00:11:07.960
How can guns be effective
against the steel-skinned Kel-Bear?

00:11:08.510 --> 00:11:10.470
Cards on the table, those bullets

00:11:10.550 --> 00:11:12.840
make use of a metal that
our company discovered in Magmell--

00:11:12.930 --> 00:11:14.010
Not that.

00:11:15.140 --> 00:11:17.970
I'm wondering why Kel-Bears
would attack a research facility.

00:11:18.270 --> 00:11:21.350
Well, that's because
they're savages, of course.

00:11:25.570 --> 00:11:27.030
Have no fear.

00:11:27.530 --> 00:11:30.570
Miss, if the need arises,
our ace in the hole is ready to go.

00:12:00.640 --> 00:12:02.600
<i>A Squad reporting. Targets neutralized.</i>

00:12:03.650 --> 00:12:06.650
<i>C Squad, one wounded,</i>
<i>but targets neutralized.</i>

00:12:09.030 --> 00:12:10.320
A favorable outcome.

00:12:18.490 --> 00:12:20.450
Professor, it seems we're saved.

00:12:21.160 --> 00:12:22.000
Yes.

00:12:28.880 --> 00:12:29.710
<i>Sir...</i>

00:12:30.920 --> 00:12:31.760
Right.

00:12:32.550 --> 00:12:33.380
It's here.

00:12:34.550 --> 00:12:35.800
Send me the feed.

00:12:36.340 --> 00:12:37.180
<i>Roger.</i>

00:12:41.600 --> 00:12:44.020
That's a... Skel-Gargon!

00:12:45.060 --> 00:12:47.560
Why is the Seventh Ward's Controller here?

00:12:47.980 --> 00:12:50.020
The Kel-Bear blood lured it over.

00:13:16.090 --> 00:13:18.640
How do we deal with this?

00:13:22.770 --> 00:13:25.060
<i>Unidentified airborne objects</i>
<i>approaching at high speed!</i>

00:13:31.270 --> 00:13:34.070
Boulders? Why are there
boulders flying at us?

00:13:34.650 --> 00:13:37.910
To a Skel-Gargon,
they might as well be baseballs.

00:13:43.200 --> 00:13:45.790
Pivot right at full speed!
Prepare to fire artillery at once!

00:13:49.750 --> 00:13:52.170
Damn! Will we have to
use our ace in the hole?

00:13:56.470 --> 00:13:57.970
The Dragon Breath Piercing Shell Bomb!

00:13:59.840 --> 00:14:00.680
No!

00:14:07.020 --> 00:14:08.270
Retreat at full speed!

00:14:09.020 --> 00:14:12.730
-Hold on! At this rate...
-Everyone, confirm death.

00:14:12.820 --> 00:14:13.820
How awful!

00:14:18.950 --> 00:14:19.990
What are you doing?

00:14:21.620 --> 00:14:22.490
Grab on.

00:14:24.830 --> 00:14:27.000
You're here to save
your father, aren't you?

00:14:47.640 --> 00:14:50.310
Who the hell is that kid?

00:15:01.530 --> 00:15:03.410
Zero, report on his condition.

00:15:04.200 --> 00:15:05.030
<i>Roger.</i>

00:15:09.460 --> 00:15:13.460
-Will this thing move?
-If I can just activate it, sure.

00:15:14.630 --> 00:15:16.960
If you want to save your father,
make it move.

00:15:20.300 --> 00:15:21.470
You sure about this?

00:15:43.990 --> 00:15:44.950
<i>What is this?</i>

00:15:53.040 --> 00:15:53.920
Which one...

00:15:54.670 --> 00:15:55.840
should die?

00:15:57.210 --> 00:15:58.920
Hey! What are you doing?

00:16:00.380 --> 00:16:04.930
Have you ever wondered why
Magmell appeared in this world?

00:16:06.720 --> 00:16:10.100
It's because the world
was just too boring.

00:16:28.780 --> 00:16:30.830
Testing.

00:16:31.830 --> 00:16:36.330
Attention researchers...
Or should I say kidnappers?

00:16:36.540 --> 00:16:38.840
Please release your hostage.

00:16:39.090 --> 00:16:41.340
You will all be saved if you do.

00:16:43.220 --> 00:16:44.050
Professor!

00:16:49.390 --> 00:16:52.060
Now, how will the pieces fall?

00:16:57.610 --> 00:16:58.650
<i>That boy...</i>

00:16:59.820 --> 00:17:00.650
<i>Shuin!</i>

00:17:02.190 --> 00:17:05.110
-We will meet your demands!
-Professor?

00:17:08.660 --> 00:17:11.620
We're... releasing the children.

00:17:18.420 --> 00:17:19.630
Seems you're in luck.

00:18:00.130 --> 00:18:02.170
-Fire!
-Okay!

00:18:09.140 --> 00:18:10.720
<i>Without a control mechanism!</i>

00:18:14.470 --> 00:18:16.390
Sorry. Today...

00:18:17.230 --> 00:18:19.850
your luck happened to run out.

00:18:34.830 --> 00:18:35.660
Inyo...

00:18:36.790 --> 00:18:37.620
Inyo!

00:18:49.510 --> 00:18:50.340
No...

00:18:56.680 --> 00:18:58.350
Inyo...

00:18:59.520 --> 00:19:00.520
Stay here.

00:19:46.440 --> 00:19:49.650
The Kel-Bears were
trying to save their children.

00:19:53.030 --> 00:19:55.030
The blood of baby Kel-Bears

00:19:55.410 --> 00:19:58.160
can be refined into
the hardest metal in existence.

00:19:59.200 --> 00:20:01.000
It's patented by Kyokusei.

00:20:02.210 --> 00:20:06.250
You killed the parents with bullets
made from their children's blood?

00:20:06.630 --> 00:20:07.630
How crass.

00:20:08.050 --> 00:20:09.760
Shut your mouth, you pipsqueak!

00:20:19.220 --> 00:20:20.220
Wait.

00:20:21.100 --> 00:20:23.440
Are you... Shuin's...?

00:20:25.650 --> 00:20:27.770
Go greet your daughter.

00:20:34.950 --> 00:20:37.700
A FEW DAYS LATER

00:20:37.780 --> 00:20:40.370
<i>It crashed due to unknown circumstances,</i>

00:20:40.750 --> 00:20:42.660
<i>but there were no reported casualties.</i>

00:20:46.830 --> 00:20:50.050
My father said he won't be
doing work in Magmell anymore.

00:20:50.630 --> 00:20:51.670
It's for the best.

00:21:18.620 --> 00:21:21.700
-Hey, Zero...
-<i>What is it, sir?</i>

00:21:23.700 --> 00:21:25.710
I think you'll grow one day.

00:21:28.420 --> 00:21:29.460
You too.

00:21:32.590 --> 00:21:33.590
That's right.

00:23:11.020 --> 00:23:12.100
PREVIEW

00:23:12.190 --> 00:23:15.900
<i>Why do people put themselves</i>
<i>in harm's way to go to Magmell?</i>

00:23:16.530 --> 00:23:18.690
<i>Because they want to become rich.</i>

00:23:18.780 --> 00:23:20.360
<i>Is that the reason?</i>

00:23:20.450 --> 00:23:22.530
<i>That's how greed works.</i>

00:23:23.120 --> 00:23:26.080
<i>By the way, Zero,</i>
<i>what's that you're eating there?</i>

00:23:26.490 --> 00:23:28.290
<i>-Pudding.</i>
<i>-Where's mine?</i>

00:23:28.370 --> 00:23:32.040
<i>Right here. But I want</i>
<i>to eat more, so it's not for you.</i>

00:23:32.630 --> 00:23:34.670
<i>-What?</i>
<i>-That's greed.</i>

00:23:36.000 --> 00:23:37.710
<i>Next time, "A Seven Color Pigeon."</i>

00:23:37.880 --> 00:23:39.380
<i>You should watch while eating pudding.</i>

00:23:39.470 --> 00:23:41.970
Subtitle translation by Keith McAbee
